cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Weyl's boundary-layer theorems formalised in Lean 4: existence and uniqueness for the Blasius and Homann problems, existence for the problems (A_lambda)"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalisation of H. Weyl, "On the differential equations of the
  simplest boundary-layer problems", Annals of Mathematics 43 (1942), 381-407.
  Section 2: existence, uniqueness, monotonicity, decay and asymptotics for the Blasius
  problem w''' + 2 w w'' = 0, w(0) = w'(0) = 0, w'(z) -> k. Section 3: the equation of
  arbitrary order with general initial data and the wake problem of Goldstein.
  Sections 6-8: the auxiliary theorem, Lemmas 1, 2 and 5, the fixed-point principle, and
  existence for w''' + 2 w w'' + 2 lambda (k^2 - w'^2) = 0, w(0) = w'(0) = 0,
  w'(z) -> k, for all lambda >= 0. The fixed-point theorem of Brouwer is taken from the
  Lean 4 formalisation harfe/fixed-point-theorems-lean4. Sections 4-5: for lambda = 1/2
  (Homann's problem) the operator Psi, convergence of Weyl's alternating iteration and
  uniqueness of the solution. Lemmas 3 and 4 and the theorem of p. 406 with monotonicity
  and Gaussian decay; numerical constants (B >= 1.287, alpha < 0.685, q2 <= 3/4).
  The Lean code was generated with
  the AI assistant Claude (Anthropic) and is verified by the Lean kernel.
